  "narrative": {
    "intro": "The Department of Veterans Affairs obligated $79.6B on contracts in FY2026 to date. The agency issued 68,016 awards with an average award size of $1.2M, and obligations are up 1.6% year over year. Contracting trends show steady growth from prior fiscal years: FY21 obligations were $47.7B, FY22 obligations were $56.4B, FY23 obligations were $61.7B, FY24 obligations were $66.9B, and FY25 obligations were $78.3B. Health-related purchases dominate spending. Direct Health and Medical Insurance Carriers received $30.6B, Pharmaceutical Preparation Manufacturing received $12.3B, and Offices of Physicians (except Mental Health Specialists) received $7.8B in FY2026 to date. The vendor landscape concentrates large shares with a few firms. OPTUM PUBLIC SECTOR SOLUTIONS, INC. received $19.9B, MCKESSON CORPORATION received $12B, and TRIWEST HEALTHCARE ALLIANCE CORP received $11B in FY2026 to date. This profile covers federal contract obligations through the current fiscal year to date and reflects partial-year totals.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "What are the biggest categories of VA contract spending in FY2026 to date?",
        "body": "Direct Health and Medical Insurance Carriers is the largest category with $30.6B in obligations. Pharmaceutical Preparation Manufacturing and Offices of Physicians (except Mental Health Specialists) are the next largest categories with $12.3B and $7.8B respectively. Computer Systems Design Services and Commercial and Institutional Building Construction follow with $4.9B and $3.5B."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Who are the largest contractors to the VA in FY2026 to date?",
        "body": "OPTUM PUBLIC SECTOR SOLUTIONS, INC. is the largest vendor with $19.9B in obligations. MCKESSON CORPORATION and TRIWEST HEALTHCARE ALLIANCE CORP follow with $12B and $11B respectively. Other top contractors include QTC MEDICAL SERVICES INC at $2.3B and ORACLE HEALTH GOVERNMENT SERVICES, INC. at $2.1B."
      }
    ]
  },
  "faq": [
    {
      "q": "How much does Department of Veterans Affairs spend on contracts?",
      "a": "The Department of Veterans Affairs obligated $79.6B on contracts in FY2026 to date. The agency issued 68,016 awards with an average award size of $1.2M, and obligations are up 1.6% year over year. FY21 through FY25 obligations were $47.7B, $56.4B, $61.7B, $66.9B, and $78.3B respectively."
    },
    {
      "q": "What does Veterans Affairs buy?",
      "a": "The Department of Veterans Affairs buys primarily health-related services and products. Direct Health and Medical Insurance Carriers received $30.6B, Pharmaceutical Preparation Manufacturing received $12.3B, and Offices of Physicians (except Mental Health Specialists) received $7.8B in FY2026 to date. The agency also buys IT services and construction, including Computer Systems Design Services at $4.9B and Commercial and Institutional Building Construction at $3.5B."
    },
    {
      "q": "Who are Veterans Affairs's largest contractors?",
      "a": "OPTUM PUBLIC SECTOR SOLUTIONS, INC. is the largest contractor to the Department of Veterans Affairs with $19.9B in obligations in FY2026 to date. Other top contractors include MCKESSON CORPORATION at $12B and TRIWEST HEALTHCARE ALLIANCE CORP at $11B. QTC MEDICAL SERVICES INC and ORACLE HEALTH GOVERNMENT SERVICES, INC. are also top vendors at $2.3B and $2.1B respectively."
